{{documentation}}

The Map template is used to easily create interactive maps or inline links to interactive maps. To find coordinates of a specific map square, use a tool such as https://mejrs.github.io/osrs. For a guide on how to manually define maps, see [[RuneScape:Create Map]].

=Map options=
===Location===

The map's centre is defined by [[#arg-map-x|<code>x</code>]] and [[#arg-map-y|<code>y</code>]] coordinates or custom features. A map with no coordinates or features will default to Lumbridge.

{| class="center"
! style="width: 50svh" | Default !! style="width: 50svh" | Placed
|-
| <code><nowiki>{{Map}}</nowiki></code>
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|x=3165|y=3494}}</nowiki></code>
|-
| {{Map}}
| {{Map|x=3165|y=3494}}
|}

===Zoom, plane and mapID===

[[#arg-map-zoom|<code>zoom</code>]] —  Overrides the automatic calculated zoom. Higher numbers result in a greater zoom.

[[#arg-feat-plane|<code>plane</code>]] — Sets the plane (or floor) for a specific feature (by [[RuneScape:Style_guide#Floor_numbering|British floor numbering]]). Features can be defined on different planes on the same map.

[[#arg-map-mapid|<code>mapID</code>]] — Sets the predefined area of the [[World map]], such as a dungeon, for an entire Map instance. A list of all possible mapIDs can be found at [[RuneScape:Map/mapIDs]], with centre points for each ID. Defaults to <code>0</code>, rendering only Gielinor's surface.

Features on a single Map cannot span multiple <code>mapID</code>s. If this is needed, use [[#Grouping|grouping]] across multiple Maps on the same page each with a different <code>mapID</code>.

{| class="center"
! style="width: 33svh" | Zoom 0 !! style="width: 33svh" | {{Floor|uk=2}} of Lumbridge Castle !! style="width: 33svh" | [[Tolna's Rift]]
|-
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|zoom=0}}</nowiki></code>
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|plane=2}}</nowiki></code>
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|mapID=21|3104,5280}}</nowiki></code>
|-
| {{Map|zoom=0}}
| {{Map|plane=2}}
| {{Map|mapID=21|3104,5280}}
|}

