===Maplinks===

Any map can be rendered as a link instead of inline by setting [[#arg-map-type|<code>type</code>]] to <code>maplink</code>. With this, [[#arg-map-text|<code>text</code>]] is used to change the text of the link.

{| class="center"
|-
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|type=maplink}}</nowiki></code><br>
{{Map|type=maplink}}
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|type=maplink|text=Maplink Text}}</nowiki></code><br>
{{Map|type=maplink|text=Maplink Text}}
|-
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|type=maplink|text=}}</nowiki></code><br>
{{Map|type=maplink|text=}}
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|type=maplink|mtype=pin|2613,3294}}</nowiki></code><br>
{{Map|type=maplink|mtype=pin|2613,3294|group=maplinks}}
|}

=Features=

Map features are defined with an [[#arg-feat-mtype|<code>mtype</code>]] and require one or more coordinates to be valid.

==Single-point==

With [[#def-single-point-feature|single-point features]], multiple coordinates will produce multiple of one type of feature.

===Pins===

Pins are commonly used to mark things that take up a 1x1 space or otherwise have an exact X/Y location.

Pins have a strict set of colour values, changed by setting [[#arg-pin-icon|<code>icon</code>]] to either <code>greenPin</code>, <code>redPin</code>, <code>bluePin</code>, <code>cyanPin</code>, <code>magentaPin</code>, <code>yellowPin</code> or <code>greyPin</code>.

{| class="center"
! style="width: 50svh" | Pin !! style="width: 50svh" | Magenta Pins
|-
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|mtype=pin|2965,3381}}</nowiki></code>
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|mtype=pin|icon=magentaPin|2638,3300|2661,3308}}</nowiki></code>
|-
| {{Map|mtype=pin|2965,3381|group=pins}}
| {{Map|mtype=pin|icon=magentaPin|2638,3300|2661,3308|group=pins2}}
|}

===Dots===

Like pins, dots are also used to mark precise locations. However, dots are better suited for marking many tightly packed coordinates.

{| class="center"
! Dots
|-
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|mtype=dot|1843,3728|1847,3728</nowiki></code><br><code><nowiki>|1851,3728 ... }}</nowiki></code>
|-
| {{Map|mtype=dot|1843,3728|1847,3728|1851,3728|1851,3724|1851,3720|1847,3720|1843,3720|group=dots}}
|}

===Circles, squares and rectangles===

Circles and squares are defined by a centre point and a radius [[#arg-feat-r|<code>r</code>]].

For squares, <code>r</code> defines half the length of the square's edges—i.e., the shortest distance from its centre to one of its edges.

Rectangles are also defined by a single point, though its side lengths are defined with [[#arg-rect-x|<code>rectX</code>]] and [[#arg-rect-y|<code>rectY</code>]].

{| class="center"
! style="width: 33svh" | Circle !! style="width: 33svh" | Square !! style="width: 33svh" | Rectangle
|-
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|mtype=circle|r=18|3165,3490}}</nowiki></code>
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|mtype=square|r=5.5|2253,2925}}</nowiki></code>
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|mtype=rectangle|rectX=21|rectY=30|3363,3310}}</nowiki></code>
|-
| {{Map|mtype=circle|r=18|3165,3490|group=circle}}
| {{Map|mtype=square|r=5.5|2253,2925|group=square}}
| {{Map|mtype=rectangle|rectX=21|rectY=30|3363,3310|group=rectangle}}
|}

===Text===

A text feature is another way to mark a precise location but with a [[#arg-text-label|<code>label</code>]] describing the subject. Though there are [[#Popups|configurable popups]], a text feature provides a more immediate and obvious label for something.

[[#arg-text-position|<code>position</code>]] — Controls the placement of the text relative to the provided point.

{| class="center"
! style="width: 50svh" | '''Default''' !! style="width: 50svh" | '''Right aligned'''
|-
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|mtype=text|2512,3466|label=Dead tree}}</nowiki></code>
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|mtype=text|2802,3005|label={{fairycode|ckr}}</nowiki></code><br><code><nowiki>|position=right}}</nowiki></code>
|-
| {{Map|mtype=text|2512,3466|label=Dead tree|group=text}}
| {{Map|mtype=text|2802,3005|label={{fairycode|ckr}}|position=right|group=text2}}
|}

===RuneScape map text===

Replicates the text style seen on the in-game [[World map]].

The text's [[#arg-rstext-colour|<code>colour</code>]], [[#arg-rstext-weight|<code>weight</code>]] and [[#arg-rstext-fontSize|<code>fontsize</code>]] are all configurable. In cases where text is hard to read due to placement, a [[#arg-rstext-bg|<code>background</code>]] colour can be supplied.

