==Multi-point==
===Lines and polygons===

Lines and polygons are defined with a series of coordinates. Unlike lines, polygons are automatically closed — i.e., the start and end points are attached.

Each point of a line is '''centered''' on its respective tile because lines should represent points that a player can stand on. 

Polygons, however, have points aligned to the '''south-west corner''' of their respective tile, allowing map locations to be outlined exactly.

{| class="center"
! style="width: 50svh" | Line !! style="width: 50svh" | Polygon 
|-
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|mtype=line|2728,3349|2726,3347|2722,3347 ... }}</nowiki></code>
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|mtype=polygon|2721,3387|2719,3385|2719,3364 ... }}</nowiki></code>
|-
|{{Map|mtype=line|2728,3349|2726,3347|2722,3347|2721,3346|2712,3346|2710,3344|2710,3342|2709,3341|2707,3341|2704,3338|2704,3337|2703,3336|2703,3334|2699,3330|2699,3328|group=line}}
|{{Map|mtype=polygon|2721,3387|2719,3385|2719,3364|2721,3362|2726,3362|2726,3350|2732,3350|2732,3362|2737,3362|2739,3364|2739,3385|2737,3387|group=polygon}}
|-
|}

===Highlighted and focused areas===

Highlighted areas are useful for emphasizing a location, de-emphasizing the surrounding area, and keep the location's contents visible.

Focused areas extend this by completely blacking out the surrounding area; this can be especially useful for hiding unrelated map locations when <code>mapID</code> is <code>-1</code>.

These feature types otherwise have the same functionality as polygons.

{| class="center"
! style="width: 50svh" | Highlighted area !! style="width: 50svh" | Focused area
|-
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|mtype=highlightedarea|2557,3334|2557,3265</nowiki></code><br><code><nowiki>|2511,3265| ... }}</nowiki></code>
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|mapID=-1|mtype=focusarea|3039,4850|3055.5,4842</nowiki></code><br><code><nowiki>|3055.5,4822| ... }}</nowiki></code>
|-
|{{Map|mtype=highlightedarea|2557,3334|2557,3265|2511,3265|2511,3280|2461,3280|2461,3306|2434,3306|2434,3322|2464,3322|2464,3334|group=highlight}}
|{{Map|mapID=-1|mtype=focusarea|3039,4850|3055.5,4842|3055.5,4822|3040,4814|3022,4822|3022,4839|group=focus}}
|}

==Combos==

Combo features are a combination of a [[#def-single-point-feature|single-point feature]] and a [[#def-multi-point-feature|multi-point feature]]. One example is <code>pin-line</code>, where <code>pin</code> is the single-point feature and <code>line</code> is the multi-point feature. Combos will generate a single-point feature per coordinate and a multi-point feature using all coordinates together.

{| class="center"
! style="width: 50svh" | Pins and polygon !! style="width: 50svh" | Dots and line
|-
| <pre><nowiki>{{Map|mtype=rstext-highlightedarea
|2774,3469,label:text1
|2784,3459,label:text2
|2794,3469,label:text3
|2784,3479,label:text4}}</pre>
| <pre>{{Map|mtype=pin-line 
|2764,3468,icon:redPin
|2764,3461,icon:yellowPin
|2771,3458,icon:greenPin
|2773,3452,icon:bluePin}}</pre>
|-
| {{Map|zoom=3|mtype=rstext-highlightedarea|group=combo1
|2774,3469,label:text1
|2784,3459,label:text2
|2794,3469,label:text3
|2784,3479,label:text4}}
| {{Map|zoom=3|mtype=pin-line|group=combo2 
|2764,3468,icon:redPin
|2764,3461,icon:yellowPin
|2771,3458,icon:greenPin
|2773,3452,icon:bluePin}}
|}

Combos should be used sparingly and only when multiple coordinates have some kind of relationship. A good example is the map of tasks throughout [[One Small Favour#Walkthrough|One Small Favour]], where the tasks must be completed in a specific order. Another example is the map of [[Canoe Station|canoe stations]], where each station represents a point along the River Lum.

Note that using a highlighted or focused area as the multi-point feature will inherently make all other features appear highlighted or focused as well.

==Properties==
===Colour, opacity and stroke width===

The stroke and fill of any features that have them can be changed with [[#arg-feat-stroke|<code>stroke</code>]] and [[#arg-feat-fill|<code>fill</code>]] using hex colour code values.

The opacity of these are controlled with [[#arg-feat-strokeOpacity|<code>stroke-opacity</code>]] and [[#arg-feat-fillOpacity|<code>fill-opacity</code>]], where <code>0</code> is transparent and <code>1</code> is opaque.

Stroke widths are controlled with [[#arg-feat-strokeWidth|<code>stroke-width</code>]] in pixels.

{| class="center"
! style="width: 50svh" | Yellow rectangle !! style="width: 50svh" | Thin red line
|-
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|zoom=3|mtype=rectangle|rectX=6|rectY=8|fill=#f0ff00</nowiki></code><br><code><nowiki>|stroke-opacity=0.6|stroke=#F6B845|stroke-width=5|1883,33161}}</nowiki></code>
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|mtype=line|stroke=#FF0000|stroke-width=1.5</nowiki></code><br><code><nowiki>|2912,3213|2888,3213|2888,3321|2843,3321}}</nowiki></code>
|-
|{{Map|zoom=3|mtype=rectangle|rectX=6|rectY=8|fill=#f0ff00|stroke-opacity=0.6|stroke=#F6B845|stroke-width=5|1883,3316|group=circle23}}
|{{Map|mtype=line|stroke=#FF0000|stroke-width=1.5|2912,3213|2888,3213|2888,3321|2843,3321|group=ehbfuksdbf}}
|-
|}

