===Popups===

By default, all features are clickable to show their X/Y coordinates. For [[#def-multi-point-feature|multi-point features]], this coordinate is the first coordinate provided. However, more details can be added.
* Add a title with [[#arg-popup-title|<code>title</code>]]. 
* Add a description with [[#arg-popup-desc|<code>desc</code>]]. 

{| class="center"
! style="width: 50svh" | Title !! style="width: 50svh" | Description
|-
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|mtype=pin|2638,3300|2661,3308|title=[[Mos Le'Water]]}}</nowiki></code>
| <code><nowiki>{{Map|mtype=media|2571,3909|img=Macaroni Penguin.png</nowiki></code><br><code><nowiki>|size=28px|desc=[[Macaroni Penguin]]}}</nowiki></code>
|-
| {{Map|zoom=1|mtype=rstext|3901,2974|label=Mos<br>Le'Water|title=[[Mos Le'Water]]|group=popup1}}
| {{Map|mtype=media|2571,3912|img=Macaroni Penguin.png|size=28px|desc=[[Macaroni Penguin]]|group=media2333}}
|}

* Add '''detailed info''' with [[#arg-popup-ptype|<code>ptype</code>]] if the feature represents an <code>item</code>, <code>monster</code>, <code>object</code> or <code>npc</code>.
** For any <code>ptype</code>, the subject's name will default to the current page's title. Set [[#arg-popup-name|<code>name</code>]] to change this. Specify the subject's internal ID with [[#arg-popup-id|<code>id</code>]] if needed.
** For monsters and NPCs, set [[#arg-popup-levels|<code>levels</code>]] and [[#arg-popup-respawn|<code>respawn</code>]] time if needed.
** For items, set [[#arg-popup-qty|<code>qty</code>]] and <code>respawn</code> time if needed.

