=Advanced usage=
===Anonymous features===

Multiple map features can be defined through [[#def-anonymous-feature|anonymous features]], which have the general form:

<code>|option1:value1,optionN:valueN,x1:y1,xN:yN</code>

You can provide as many options and coordinates as you want for a single anonymous feature. Each option/value and x/y must be separated by a colon (<code>:</code>), and each of these pairings must be separated by a comma (<code>,</code>).

The options available to use in anonymous features are exactly the same as regular [[#Feature options|named arguments]], meaning the two are entirely interchangeable. If a named argument is also provided as an anonymous argument, the anonymous value will override the named value.

One small difference with anonymous features—because they are comma- and colon-separated—is the need to escape ''extra'' commas and colons with <code>\</code> backslashes in certain options. These are mentioned in the table of [[#Feature options|feature options]] below.

{| class="center"
|-
| <code><nowiki>|mtype:rstext,3211:3247,label:A comma \,<br>and a colon \:</nowiki></code><br><code><nowiki>|mtype:pin,3246:3248,desc:A comma \,<br>and a colon \:</nowiki></code>
|-
|{{Map|mtype:rstext,3211:3247,label:A comma \,<br>and a colon \:
|mtype:pin,3246:3248,desc:A comma \,<br>and a colon \:|group=anonfeats}}
|}

Because the anonymous feature syntax is used solely to create features, [[#Map options|map-only options]] cannot be used as feature options.

===Transclusion===

Many maps that contain a large number of features (or are otherwise complex and lengthy) are sometimes defined on their own under the [https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Special:PrefixIndex?namespace=118 Map] namespace and then [https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Transclusion transcluded] in another page.

