===Bucket===

By default the Map module provides functionality that allows other pages, templates, and modules to interact with its data. More specifically, the final map options and GeoJSON for each feature will be stored in bucket for other resources to consume. See [[Bucket:Map]] for example data.

In some cases, a page will have multiple maps that relate to specific instances of the page's subject. For example, [[Forestry Shop]] has three maps that each relate to one of its locations. To handle this, you can set  <code>bucketName</code> to tell the Map module to store each map in a separate Bucket entry under the page; Otherwise, each of the maps would overwrite each other. The value of <code>bucketName</code> should match the subject's instance name if possible ("Draynor Village", "Seers' Village", or "Prifddinas" in the Forestry Shop example).

=Arguments=
==Map options==

Map options are [[#def-named-argument|named arguments]] that define how the map itself behaves and how it is rendered on the page. These options cannot be used as feature options.

{{ArgDocHeader}}
{{ArgDocLine
|name = type
|description = Sets the map type on the page.
|values = <code>mapframe</code> <code>maplink</code>
|default = <code>mapframe</code>
|id = map-type
}}
{{ArgDocLine
|name = width
|description = Sets the map width on the page.
|values = Any number >=<code>1</code>
|default = <code>300</code>
|id = map-width
}}
{{ArgDocLine
|name = height
|description = Sets the map height on the page.
|values = Any number >=<code>1</code>
|default = <code>300</code>
|id = map-height
}}
{{ArgDocLine
|name = align
|description = Sets the map's alignment on the page.
|values = <code>left</code> <code>center</code> <code>right</code>
|default = <code>center</code>
|id = align
}}
{{ArgDocLine
|name = x
|description = Sets the X coordinate of the map view if at least one feature is defined.
|values = Any number >=<code>0</code>
|default = <code>3233</code>
|id = map-x
}}
{{ArgDocLine
|name = y
|description = Sets the Y coordinate of the map view if at least one feature is defined.
|values = Any number >=<code>0</code>
|default = <code>3222</code>
|id = map-y
}}
{{ArgDocLine
|name = zoom
|description = Sets the zoom amount. A higher number means a closer zoom.
|values = Any integer <code>-3</code>–<code>5</code>
|default = <code>2</code>
|id = map-zoom
}}
{{ArgDocLine
|name = mapID
|description = Sets the map ID.
|values = Any [[RuneScape:Map/mapIDs|map ID]]
|default = <code>0</code>
|id = map-mapid
}}
{{ArgDocLine
|name = caption
|description = Adds a caption to the map if <code>type</code> is unset or set to <code>mapframe</code>.
|values = Any text
|id = map-caption
}}
{{ArgDocLine
|name = text
|description = If <code>type</code> is set to <code>maplink</code>, changes the text of the link.
|values = Any text
|id = map-text
}}
{{ArgDocLine
|name = nopreprocess
|description = Outputs the final map element with GeoJSON as raw text instead of a rendered map.
|values = <code>True</code>
}}
{{ArgDocFooter}}

==Feature options==

Feature options are [[#def-named-argument|named]] or [[#def-anonymous-argument|anonymous]] arguments that define features on the map.

{{ArgDocHeader}}
{{ArgDocLine
|name = mtype
|description = Sets the type of a feature.
|values = <code>pin</code> <code>rectangle</code> <code>square</code> <code>circle</code> <code>dot</code> <code>text</code> <code>rstext</code> <code>media</code> <code>line</code> <code>polygon</code> <code>highlightedarea</code> <code>focusarea</code> or a [[#def-combo-feature|combo type]]
|default = <code>pin</code>
|id = feat-mtype
}}
{{ArgDocLine
|name = x
|description = Sets the X coordinate of a feature. Can also be set with [[#def-coordinate-shorthand|coordinate shorthand]].
|values = Any number >=<code>0</code>
|default = <code>3233</code>
}}
{{ArgDocLine
|name = y
|description = Sets the Y coordinate of a feature. Can also be set with [[#def-coordinate-shorthand|coordinate shorthand]].
|values = Any number >=<code>0</code>
|default = <code>3222</code>
}}
{{ArgDocLine
|name = plane
|description = Sets the plane (Z value) a feature is on.
|values = Any integer <code>0</code>–<code>3</code>
|default = <code>0</code>
|id = feat-plane
}}
{{ArgDocLine
|name = stroke
|description = Sets the stroke color of a feature with a stroke.
|values = Any hexadecimal color code
|default = <code>#3388ff</code>
|id = feat-stroke
}}
{{ArgDocLine
|name = stroke-opacity
|description = Sets the stroke opacity of a feature with a stroke.
|values = Any number <code>0</code>–<code>1</code>
|default = <code>1</code>
|id = feat-strokeOpacity
}}
{{ArgDocLine
|name = stroke-width
|description = Sets the stroke width of a feature with a stroke.
|values = Any number >=<code>0</code>
|default = <code>3</code>
|id = feat-strokeWidth
}}
{{ArgDocLine
|name = fill
|description = Sets the fill color of a feature with a fill.
|values = Any hexadecimal color code
|default = <code>#3388ff</code>
|id = feat-fill
}}
{{ArgDocLine
|name = fill-opacity
|description = Sets the fill opacity of a feature with a fill.
|values = Any number <code>0</code>–<code>1</code>
