==Bucket options==

{{ArgDocHeader}}
{{ArgDocLine
|name = bucket
|description = Enables [[Bucket:Map|Bucket data]] for the current page. This should only be used if the map directly relates to the page subject. See [[#Bucket|Bucket]] for more info.
|values = <code>yes</code> <code>hist</code> <code>both</code>
|default = yes
}}
{{ArgDocLine
|name = bucketName
|description = A subpage name used to store a specific instance of a page in Bucket. This should only be used if the map does ''not'' directly describe the page subject. See [[#Bucket|Bucket]] for more info.
|values = Any subpage name
}}
{{ArgDocLine
|name = fromBucket
|description = A page or subpage name to pull from [[Bucket:Map|Bucket]] and build a fully rendered map. No provided feature options will be processed. Any provided map options will combine with or override the page's map options.
|values = Any page or subpage name
}}
{{ArgDocFooter}}

=Definitions=

* <div id="def-named-argument" /> '''Named argument''' - An argument with the form <code>|arg=value</code>.
** <div id="def-named-feature" /> '''Named feature''' - A feature defined entirely with named arguments.
* <div id="def-anonymous-argument" /> '''Anonymous argument''' - An argument with the form <code>|value</code>.
** <div id="def-anonymous-feature" /> '''Anonymous feature''' - A feature defined entirely or partially with anonymous arguments. Uses the format <code>|option1:value1,optionN:valueN,x1:y1,xN:yN</code>.
* <div id="def-single-point-feature" /> '''Single-point feature''' - A feature defined by a single point.
** pin, rectangle, square, circle, dot, text, rstext, media
* <div id="def-multi-point-feature" /> '''Multi-point feature''' - A feature defined by multiple points.
** line, polygon, highlightedarea, focusarea
* <div id="def-combo-feature" /> '''Combo feature''' - A feature that combines a ''single-point'' feature with a ''multi-point'' feature. Examples: <code>pin-line</code>, <code>dot-line</code>, and <code>pin-polygon</code>.
* <div id="def-coordinate-shorthand" /> '''Coordinate shorthand''' - A more compact way to provide X/Y coordinates for a feature. Allows multiple coordinates to be provided.
** For ''named features'', this could look like <code>|1000,1000|2000,2000</code>.
** For ''anonymous features'', this could look like <code>|1000:1000,2000:2000</code>.

=Cleanup tasks=

* Many uses of this template still use <code>squareX</code> and <code>squareY</code> to define both squares and rectangles. These options are still supported in the code only as a backwards compatibility measure. Any uses of these should be changed to <code>rectX</code> and <code>rectY</code> respectively.
** If these numbers '''do''' match, switch these options out with <code>r</code> and ensure the <code>mtype</code> is <code>square</code>.
** If these numbers '''don't''' match, the <code>mtype</code> should be changed to <code>rectangle</code>.

